      ],
      "source": "https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Southwick%2C_Massachusetts"
    },
    {
      "id": 2,
      "text": "The New Haven and Northampton Company's railroad, finished in the late 1840s, ran beside the old canal that had been abandoned due to winter freezes and beaver dams.",
      "sourceSentenceIds": [
        9,
        10
      ],
      "sourceLabels": [
        "Wikipedia"
      ],
      "source": "https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Southwick%2C_Massachusetts"
    },
    {
      "id": 3,
      "text": "Southwick's Free Public Library, founded in 1892, has been a community hub for over a century.",
      "sourceSentenceIds": [
        19
      ],
      "sourceLabels": [
        "Wikipedia"
      ],
      "source": "https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Southwick%2C_Massachusetts"
    },
    {
      "id": 4,
      "text": "The town's historic Roger Moore house, built in 1751, is being restored to become Southwick's first museum.",
      "sourceSentenceIds": [
        13
      ],
      "sourceLabels": [
        "Web source 1"
      ],
      "source": "https://www.southwickma.gov/168/About-Us"
    },
    {
      "id": 5,
      "text": "Southwick Time Machine, a local history blog, started as motorcycle rides to ruins and now publishes stories online.",
